/-!
# The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient into the structure sheaf

Let `Y` be a ringed space, let `ℐ ⊂ O_Y` be a sheaf of ideals and set `O_X = O_Y/ℐ`. Writing
`𝒩 = 𝓗om_{O_Y}(ℐ/ℐ², O_X)` for the normal sheaf, [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ] asserts that for `ℐ`
Koszul-regular

`R𝓗om_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = ⋀^r 𝒩 [-r]`,

where `r` sends a point of `Y` to the minimal number of generators of `ℐ` near it. Equivalently,
the Ext sheaves `𝓔xt^i_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` vanish for `i ≠ r` and the `r`-th one is `⋀^r 𝒩`.

This file treats the coefficients `O_Y` — the structure sheaf itself, rather than the quotient —
in the Koszul computation of those Ext sheaves, for `ℐ` generated by global sections
`f₁, …, f_r` whose Koszul complex resolves `O_X`. It proves

* `𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = 0` for every `n ≠ r`, when the germs of `f₁, …, f_r` form a
  Koszul-regular sequence at every point;
* the quotient map `O_Y ⟶ O_X` induces an isomorphism
  `𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) ≅ 𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X)`.

Combined with the computation of the self-Ext sheaves of `O_X` as exterior powers of
`𝓔xt^1_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X) = 𝒩` (Stacks, Tag 0BQY) the second statement identifies `𝓔xt^r` with
`⋀^r 𝒩`.

The argument is the one of the source. The Koszul complex `K^•` is a strictly perfect resolution
of `O_X`, so `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain` computes
`𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, M)` as the `n`-th cohomology sheaf of the internal Hom complex
`𝓗om^•(K^•, M)`, naturally in `M`. Into a module `N` placed in degree zero, the degree-`k` term
of that complex is `𝓗om(⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ), N)`, and by the Leibniz rule its differential is, up to sign,
precomposition with the Koszul differential. Exactness is a stalkwise matter, and at a point `x`
the stalk of `𝓗om(⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ), N)` is `Hom_{O_x}(⋀ᵏ((O_x)ʳ), N_x)` because the exterior power is
of finite presentation, the stalk of the Koszul differential being the Koszul differential of
the germs. So at `x` the complex `𝓗om^•(K^•, O_Y)` is the dual of the Koszul complex of the germs:

* in degrees `0, …, r - 1` it is exact because the germs are Koszul-regular
  (`Koszul.dual_d_zero_eq_zero`, `Koszul.exists_dual_d_eq_of_comp_eq_zero`), and outside
  `0, …, r` it vanishes;
* in degree `r` the image of the differential consists of the functionals on `⋀^r((O_x)ʳ)` with
  values in the ideal of the germs (`Koszul.mem_span_iff_exists_dual_d_eq`), which is the kernel
  of postcomposition with `O_x ⟶ (O_X)_x`; and that postcomposition is surjective because
  `⋀^r((O_x)ʳ)` is free. Since `𝓗om^•(K^•, O_X)` has vanishing differential, the map on the
  `r`-th cohomology sheaves is an isomorphism.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.unitSingleComplex`: the coefficients `O_Y` of the
  tag, as a complex concentrated in degree zero.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.structureSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain`: the Ext sheaves
  `𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` as the cohomology sheaves of `𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y)`, which is
  the step of the proof of the tag supplied by [Stacks, Tag 08DM].
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homTermIso`: the degree-`k` term of the Hom complex
  out of the Koszul complex into `N[0]` is `𝓗om(⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ), N)`.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homTermStalkEquiv`: its stalk at `x` is
  `Hom_{O_x}(⋀ᵏ((O_x)ʳ), N_x)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc`: the Ext
  sheaves of `O_X` into `O_Y` vanish in every degree outside `0, …, r`; this needs no
  regularity of the germs.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_ne`: **the Ext sheaves
  of `O_X` into `O_Y` vanish in every degree `n ≠ r`.**
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isIso_derivedSheafExtMap_unit_quotient`: **the map
  `𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) ⟶ 𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X)` induced by `O_Y ⟶ O_X` is an isomorphism.**
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d`: at a stalk, the
  differential of the Hom complex is, up to sign, precomposition with the Koszul differential of
  the germs.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.exactAt_sheafHomComplex_unit`: the Hom complex into
  `O_Y` is exact in the degrees `0, …, r - 1`.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isIso_homologyMap_homMap_koszulQuotientπ`: the map of
  Hom complexes induced by `O_Y ⟶ O_X` is an isomorphism on the `r`-th cohomology sheaves.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain_naturality`: the
  identification of the Ext sheaves with the cohomology of the Hom complex is natural in the
  coefficients.

## Implementation notes

The ideal sheaf is given by a **global** Koszul presentation: a
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData` for a morphism `φ : (O_Y)ʳ ⟶ O_Y` sending the `k`-th
generator to the global section `f k`, with `ℐ` its image and `O_X` the quotient, whose
augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism. This is the situation after the opening reduction of the
proof of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ], "we may assume that we have global sections `f₁, …, f_r` of `O_Y`
which generate `ℐ` and which form a Koszul regular sequence"; the Koszul-regularity is assumed of
the germs at every point, which is what the stalkwise computation consumes. With a global
presentation the function `r` of the tag is the constant `r`. The isomorphism in degree `r` uses
only the presentation, not the regularity of the germs.

The degree hypothesis of `isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc` is phrased as the
disjunction `n < 0 ∨ (r : ℤ) < n` rather than as `n ∉ Set.Icc 0 (r : ℤ)`, so that the two cases
are available to `rcases` without unfolding set membership.

The term of the Koszul cochain complex in degree `-n` is the term of the Koszul chain complex in
degree `-(-n)`, definitionally and not syntactically, because `Stacks.ChainComplex.asCochain` is
a restriction along an embedding of complex shapes. The degree-`k` term of the Hom complex is
therefore read through an equality `n = k` of integers carried as an argument (`homTermIso`),
and the evaluation formulas are proved for terms renamed along arbitrary equalities, which are
then substituted away.

Signs: the differential of the Hom complex from degree `n` to degree `m = n + 1` is
precomposition with the Koszul differential after multiplying by `(-1)^m`. Exactness does not see
the sign, and the statements carry it on the Hom section, where it is a unit of `ℤ`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CP)
-/


@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex

universe u

namespace Stacks.HomologicalComplex

/-- **The map on homology induced by a surjection onto a complex with vanishing
differentials.** Let `φ : K ⟶ L` be a morphism of complexes in an abelian category, let the
differential of `K` out of degree `j` and both differentials of `L` at `j` vanish. If
`K^{j-1} ⟶ K^j ⟶ L^j` is exact and `φ_j` is an epimorphism, then `φ` induces an isomorphism
`H^j(K) ≅ H^j(L) = L^j`: both are the cokernel of `K^{j-1} ⟶ K^j`. -/
theorem isIso_homologyMap_of_exact_of_epi {C : Type*} [Category C] [Abelian C] {ι : Type*}
    {c : ComplexShape ι} {K L : HomologicalComplex C c} (φ : K ⟶ L) (j : ι)
    (hK : K.d j (c.next j) = 0) (hL₁ : L.d (c.prev j) j = 0) (hL₂ : L.d j (c.next j) = 0)
    (hex : (ShortComplex.mk (K.d (c.prev j) j) (φ.f j)
      (by rw [← φ.comm, hL₁, Limits.comp_zero])).Exact) [Epi (φ.f j)] :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ j) := by
  let γ := ShortComplex.LeftHomologyMapData.ofIsColimitCokernelCofork
    ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor C c j).map φ) hK _ hex.gIsCokernel hL₂ _
    (Limits.CokernelCofork.IsColimit.ofId _ hL₁) (𝟙 _)
    ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.comp_id _).symm)
  have : IsIso γ.φH := by change IsIso (𝟙 _); infer_instance
  change IsIso (ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor C c j).map φ))
  rw [γ.homologyMap_eq]
  infer_instance

end Stacks.HomologicalComplex

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

variable (Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u})

/-- **The Leibniz rule for the internal Hom complex into a complex concentrated in degree
zero.** The target has vanishing differential, so evaluating the differential of a Hom section
is, up to the sign `(-1)^m`, evaluating the section on the differential of the source. -/
theorem applyHomSectionOver_d_single
    (E : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
    (H : SheafHomComplex Y E
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N))
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U) {n m p p' q : ℤ} (hnm : n + 1 = m) (hp : p + 1 = p')
    (hpq : p + m = q) (s : (H.obj.X n).val.obj (op U)) (y : (E.X p).val.obj (op V)) :
    applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i m p q hpq ((H.obj.d n m).val.app (op U) s) y =
      m.negOnePow • applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i n p' q (by omega) s
        ((E.d p p').val.app (op V) y) := by
  subst hnm hp
  rw [applyHomSectionOver_differential Y H U V i n p (q - 1) q (by omega) (by omega) s y,
    HomologicalComplex.single_obj_d, Stacks.SheafOfModules.zero_val_app_apply, zero_add]

/-- An evaluation of a Hom section, transported to a fixed module `N`, does not depend on the
spelling of the target degree. -/
theorem eqToHom_applyHomSectionOver_congr
    {E L : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ}
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
    (H : SheafHomComplex Y E L)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    {n p q₁ q₂ : ℤ} (hq : q₁ = q₂) (hpq₁ : p + n = q₁) (hpq₂ : p + n = q₂) (h₁ : L.X q₁ = N)
    (h₂ : L.X q₂ = N)
    (s : (H.obj.X n).val.obj (op U)) (y : (E.X p).val.obj (op V)) :
    eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h₁)
        (applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i n p q₁ hpq₁ s y) =
      eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h₂)
        (applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i n p q₂ hpq₂ s y) := by
  subst hq
  rfl

/-- **Evaluation commutes with scaling the Hom section by a unit of `ℤ`.** -/
theorem applyHomSectionOver_units_smul_left
    {E L : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ}
    (H : SheafHomComplex Y E L)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U) (n p q : ℤ) (hpq : p + n = q) (c : ℤˣ)
    (f : (H.obj.X n).val.obj (op U)) (x : (E.X p).val.obj (op V)) :
    applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i n p q hpq (c • f) x =
      c • applyHomSectionOver Y H U V i n p q hpq f x := by
  rcases Int.units_eq_one_or c with rfl | rfl
  · rw [one_smul, one_smul]
  · rw [Units.neg_smul, Units.neg_smul, one_smul, one_smul]
    refine eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left ?_
    rw [← applyHomSectionOver_add_left, neg_add_cancel, applyHomSectionOver_zero_left]

variable [HasSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **The differential of the internal Hom complex into a complex concentrated in degree zero,
read on the terms `SheafHom(E^{-n}, N)`.** Up to the sign `(-1)^m`, carried by the Hom section,
the differential from degree `n` to degree `m = n + 1` is precomposition with the differential
`E^{-m} ⟶ E^{-n}` of the source. -/
theorem homDegreeIsoSingle_d_app_apply
    (E : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
    {n m : ℤ} (hnm : n + 1 = m)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex Y E
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj
        (op U))
    (y : ((E.X (-m)).over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N m).hom.val.app (op U)
        (((sheafHomComplex Y E
          ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d n
            m).val.app (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk i)) y =
      ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N n).hom.val.app (op U) (m.negOnePow • s)).app (op (Over.mk i))
        ((E.d (-m) (-n)).val.app (op V) y) := by
  refine (homDegreeIsoSingle_app_apply Y E N m U V i _ y).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_
    (homDegreeIsoSingle_app_apply Y E N n U V i _ ((E.d (-m) (-n)).val.app (op V) y)).symm
  refine (congrArg (fun z => eqToHom (congrArg
      (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
        (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i)))
      (show ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N).X (m - m)
        = N from by rw [sub_self]; rfl)) z)
    (applyHomSectionOver_d_single Y E N _ U V i hnm (p' := -n) (by omega) (by omega) s y)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => eqToHom (congrArg
      (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
        (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i)))
      (show ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N).X (n - n)
        = N from by rw [sub_self]; rfl)) z)
    (applyHomSectionOver_units_smul_left Y _ U V i n (-n) (n - n) (by omega) m.negOnePow s
      ((E.d (-m) (-n)).val.app (op V) y))).symm
  refine (map_zsmul _ _ _).trans (Eq.trans ?_ (map_zsmul _ _ _).symm)
  refine congrArg (fun z => (m.negOnePow : ℤ) • z) ?_
  exact eqToHom_applyHomSectionOver_congr Y N _ U V i (by omega) _ _
    (by rw [sub_self]; rfl) (by rw [sub_self]; rfl) s _

omit [HasSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- A morphism of sheaves of modules framed by two transports acts on sections as the morphism
itself, the transports becoming transports of the section types. -/
theorem eqToHom_comp_comp_eqToHom_app
    {A B N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (g : N ⟶ N')
    (e₁ : A = N) (e₂ : N' = B) (h : A = N) (h' : B = N') (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (z : (A.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h')
        ((eqToHom e₁ ≫ g ≫ eqToHom e₂).val.app (op V) z) =
      g.val.app (op V) (eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h) z) := by
  subst e₁ e₂
  rfl

omit [HasSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The component in degree `q = 0` of the map of complexes concentrated in degree zero induced
by `g : N ⟶ N'` acts on sections as `g`, up to the identification of the degree-`q` terms with
`N` and `N'`. -/
theorem eqToHom_single_map_f_app
    {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (g : N ⟶ N') {q : ℤ}
    (hq : q = 0)
    (h : ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N).X q = N)
    (h' : ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N').X q = N')
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (z : ((((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N).X q).over
      U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h')
        ((((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g).f q).val.app
          (op V) z) =
      g.val.app (op V) (eqToHom (congrArg
        (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
          (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) h) z) := by
  subst hq
  rw [single_map_f_self]
  exact eqToHom_comp_comp_eqToHom_app Y g h h'.symm h h' U V i z

/-- **Postcomposition on the internal Hom complex into a complex concentrated in degree zero,
read on the terms `SheafHom(E^{-n}, N)`.** The map of Hom complexes induced by `g : N ⟶ N'` is
postcomposition with `g`. -/
theorem homDegreeIsoSingle_homMap_app_apply
    (E : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ)
    {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (g : N ⟶ N') (n : ℤ)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex Y E
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj
        (op U))
    (y : ((E.X (-n)).over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N' n).hom.val.app (op U)
        (((homMap Y (𝟙 E)
          ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          g)).f n).val.app (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk i)) y =
      g.val.app (op V) (((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N n).hom.val.app (op U) s).app
        (op (Over.mk i)) y) := by
  refine (homDegreeIsoSingle_app_apply Y E N' n U V i _ y).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (g.val.app (op V))
    (homDegreeIsoSingle_app_apply Y E N n U V i s y).symm)
  refine (congrArg (fun z => eqToHom (congrArg
      (fun Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) =>
        (Z.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i)))
      (show ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N').X (n - n)
        = N' from by rw [sub_self]; rfl)) z)
    (applyHomSectionOver_homMap Y (𝟙 E)
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g) U V i n (-n)
      (n - n) (by omega) s y)).trans ?_
  exact eqToHom_single_map_f_app Y g (sub_self n) (by rw [sub_self]; rfl)
    (by rw [sub_self]; rfl) U V i _

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle_d_app_apply` with the terms of the source
renamed along equalities `E^{-n} = P₀`, `E^{-m} = P₁`, and its differential presented as
`δ : P₁ ⟶ P₀`. -/
theorem homDegreeIsoSingle_eqToIso_d_app_apply
    (E : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
    {n m : ℤ} (hnm : n + 1 = m)
    {P₀ P₁ : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)}
    (h₀ : E.X (-n) = P₀) (h₁ : E.X (-m) = P₁)
    (δ : P₁ ⟶ P₀) (hδ : E.d (-m) (-n) = eqToHom h₁ ≫ δ ≫ eqToHom h₀.symm)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex Y E
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj
        (op U))
    (y : (P₁.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N m ≪≫
        eqToIso (congrArg (fun P => internalHomSheaf Y P N) h₁)).hom.val.app (op U)
        (((sheafHomComplex Y E
          ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d n
            m).val.app (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk i)) y =
      ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N n ≪≫
        eqToIso (congrArg (fun P => internalHomSheaf Y P N) h₀)).hom.val.app (op U)
          (m.negOnePow • s)).app (op (Over.mk i)) (δ.val.app (op V) y) := by
  subst h₀ h₁
  simp only [eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id] at hδ
  subst hδ
  simp only [eqToIso_refl, Iso.trans_refl]
  exact homDegreeIsoSingle_d_app_apply Y E N hnm U V i s y

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle_homMap_app_apply` with the term of the
source renamed along an equality `E^{-n} = P`. -/
theorem homDegreeIsoSingle_eqToIso_homMap_app_apply
    (E : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ℤ)
    {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (g : N ⟶ N') (n : ℤ)
    {P : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (h : E.X (-n) = P)
    (U V : Y.C) (i : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((sheafHomComplex Y E
      ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj
        (op U))
    (y : (P.over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk i))) :
    ((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N' n ≪≫
        eqToIso (congrArg (fun P => internalHomSheaf Y P N') h)).hom.val.app (op U)
        (((homMap Y (𝟙 E)
          ((single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          g)).f n).val.app (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk i)) y =
      g.val.app (op V) (((homDegreeIsoSingle Y E N n ≪≫
        eqToIso (congrArg (fun P => internalHomSheaf Y P N) h)).hom.val.app (op U) s).app
          (op (Over.mk i)) y) := by
  subst h
  simp only [eqToIso_refl, Iso.trans_refl]
  exact homDegreeIsoSingle_homMap_app_apply Y E g n U V i s y

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

open Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.ChainComplex

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ}
  {A : SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)}
  {φ : koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)}

section StalkComputation

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.SheafHomStalk Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules

/-- The term of the Koszul cochain complex in degree `-n` is the `k`-th exterior power of
`(O_Y)ʳ`, for `n = k`. -/
theorem cochain_X_neg_eq (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) :
    (cochain Rc K).X (-n) = A.exteriorPower k := by
  subst h
  exact (congrArg K.chain.X (neg_neg _)).trans (K.chain_X k)

/-- The term of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex into a module `N` concentrated in
degree zero, in degree `n = k`, is `𝓗om(⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ), N)`. -/
def homTermIso (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (N : StructureSheafModules Rc) {n : ℤ}
    {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) :
    (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n ≅
      RingedSite.internalHomSheaf (ringedSite Rc) (A.exteriorPower k) N :=
  RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K) N n ≪≫
    eqToIso (congrArg (fun M => RingedSite.internalHomSheaf (ringedSite Rc) M N)
      (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h))

/-- The differential of the Koszul cochain complex from degree `-m` to degree `-n`, for
`m = k + 1` and `n = k`, is the Koszul differential `⋀^{k+1}((O_Y)ʳ) ⟶ ⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ)` up to the
identifications of the terms. -/
theorem cochain_d_neg_eq (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k)
    (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) :
    (cochain Rc K).d (-m) (-n) =
      eqToHom (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h') ≫ K.dNat k ≫ eqToHom (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h).symm := by
  have key : ∀ {p q : ℤ} (hp : p = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (hq : q = k)
      (h₁ : K.chain.X p = A.exteriorPower (k + 1)) (h₀ : K.chain.X q = A.exteriorPower k),
      K.chain.d p q = eqToHom h₁ ≫ K.dNat k ≫ eqToHom h₀.symm := by
    intro p q hp hq h₁ h₀
    subst hp hq
    exact chain_d_eq_dNat K k
  exact key (p := -(-m)) (q := -(-n)) (by omega) (by omega) (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h')
    (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h)

/-- **The differential of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex, on sections.** Read through
`homTermIso`, the differential from degree `k` to degree `k + 1` is, up to the sign `(-1)^m`,
precomposition with the Koszul differential `⋀^{k+1}((O_Y)ʳ) ⟶ ⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ)`. -/
theorem homTermIso_d_app_apply (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (N : StructureSheafModules Rc)
    {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (U V : Opens X) (j : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj (op U))
    (b : ((A.exteriorPower (k + 1)).over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk j))) :
    ((homTermIso Rc K N h').hom.val.app (op U)
        (((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
          ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d n m).val.app
            (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk j)) b =
      ((homTermIso Rc K N h).hom.val.app (op U) (m.negOnePow • s)).app (op (Over.mk j))
        ((K.dNat k).val.app (op V) b) :=
  RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle_eqToIso_d_app_apply (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K) N
    (by omega) (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h) (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h') (K.dNat k)
    (cochain_d_neg_eq Rc K h h') U V j s b

/-- **Postcomposition on the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex, on sections.** Read through
`homTermIso`, the map of Hom complexes induced by `g : N ⟶ N'` is postcomposition with `g`. -/
theorem homTermIso_homMap_app_apply (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    {N N' : StructureSheafModules Rc} (g : N ⟶ N') {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (U V : Opens X)
    (j : V ⟶ U)
    (s : ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj (op U))
    (b : ((A.exteriorPower k).over U).val.obj (op (Over.mk j))) :
    ((homTermIso Rc K N' h).hom.val.app (op U)
        (((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
          ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g)).f n).val.app
            (op U) s)).app (op (Over.mk j)) b =
      g.val.app (op V) (((homTermIso Rc K N h).hom.val.app (op U) s).app (op (Over.mk j)) b) :=
  RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle_eqToIso_homMap_app_apply (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K) g n
    (cochain_X_neg_eq Rc K h) U V j s b

/-- **The stalk of a term of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex.** The stalk at `x` of
the degree-`k` term of `𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), N)` is the module of `O_x`-linear maps from
`⋀ᵏ((O_x)ʳ)` to the stalk `N_x`. -/
def homTermStalkEquiv (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (N : StructureSheafModules Rc)
    {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (x : X) :
    modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n) x ≃ₗ[
          ringStalk Rc x]
      (⋀[↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)]^k (Fin r → ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)) →ₗ[
          ringStalk Rc x] modStalk N x) :=
  have : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation.{u, u, u}
      (R := structureSheaf Rc) (A.exteriorPower k) :=
    isFinitePresentation_koszulExteriorPower Rc (A := A) k
  modStalkEquivOfIso Rc (homTermIso Rc K N h) x ≪≫ₗ
    internalHomSheafStalkEquiv Rc (A.exteriorPower k) N x ≪≫ₗ
    LinearEquiv.arrowCongr (Stacks.SheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv A k x)
      (LinearEquiv.refl (ringStalk Rc x) (modStalk N x))

/-- The stalk identification `homTermStalkEquiv` on germs: the germ of a Hom section `s`,
evaluated on the germ of a section `z` of the exterior power, is the germ of the value of `s`
on `z`. -/
theorem homTermStalkEquiv_germ (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (N : StructureSheafModules Rc)
    {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (x : X) (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (s : ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n).val.obj (op U))
    (z : (commVal (Rc := Rc) (A.exteriorPower k)).obj (op U)) :
    homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x (germAt _ U x hxU s)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv A k x
          (germAt (A.exteriorPower k) U x hxU z)) =
      germAt N U x hxU (((homTermIso Rc K N h).hom.val.app (op U) s).app
        (op (Over.mk (𝟙 U))) z) := by
  have : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation.{u, u, u}
      (R := structureSheaf Rc) (A.exteriorPower k) :=
    isFinitePresentation_koszulExteriorPower Rc (A := A) k
  rw [homTermStalkEquiv]
  simp only [LinearEquiv.trans_apply, LinearEquiv.arrowCongr_apply, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply,
    LinearEquiv.refl_apply]
  exact (congrArg (fun y => internalHomSheafStalkEquiv Rc (A.exteriorPower k) N x y
      (germAt (A.exteriorPower k) U x hxU z))
      (modStalkEquivOfIso_germ Rc (homTermIso Rc K N h) x U hxU s)).trans
    (internalHomSheafStalkEquiv_germ Rc (A.exteriorPower k) N x U hxU _ z)

/-- The wedge basis vector of the stalk of `⋀ᵏ((O_Y)ʳ)` indexed by `t` is the image under
`exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv` of the germ of the corresponding basis section. -/
private theorem wedgeBasis_eq_exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv_germ (k : ℕ) {x : X} (U : Opens X)
    (hxU : x ∈ U) (t : ↑(Set.powersetCard (Fin r) k)) :
    wedgeBasis ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r k t =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv A k x
        (germAt (A.exteriorPower k) U x hxU (exteriorBasisSection A U k (wedgeIndex k t))) :=
  (wedgeBasis_apply ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r k t).trans
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv_germ_exteriorBasisSection A k U hxU
      (wedgeIndex k t)).symm

/-- **Postcomposition on stalks.** Under `homTermStalkEquiv`, the map of stalks induced by the
map of Hom complexes `𝓗om^•(K, N) ⟶ 𝓗om^•(K, N')` of a morphism `g : N ⟶ N'` is
postcomposition with the stalk of `g`. -/
theorem homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_homMap (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    {N N' : StructureSheafModules Rc} (g : N ⟶ N') {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (x : X)
    (y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n) x) :
    homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N' h x (stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc)
        (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
          ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g)).f n).val x y) =
      stalkLin g.val x ∘ₗ homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x y := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq _ y
  have hd : stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g)).f n).val x
          (germAt _ U x hxU s) =
      germAt _ U x hxU (((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map g)).f n).val.app
          (op U) s) :=
    stalkLin_germAddHom _ U hxU s
  rw [hd]
  refine Module.Basis.ext (wedgeBasis ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r k) fun t => ?_
  rw [wedgeBasis_eq_exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv_germ Rc k U hxU, LinearMap.comp_apply,
    homTermStalkEquiv_germ]
  exact (congrArg (germAt N' U x hxU) (homTermIso_homMap_app_apply Rc K g h U U (𝟙 U) s _)).trans
    ((stalkLin_germAddHom g.val U hxU _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (stalkLin g.val x) (homTermStalkEquiv_germ Rc K N h x U hxU s _).symm))

variable (f : Fin r → ↑(Rc.obj.obj (op (⊤ : Opens ↥X))))
  (hφ : ∀ k : Fin r,
    ((SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)).freeHomEquiv φ
      (ULift.up k)).val (op (⊤ : Opens ↥X)) = f k)

include hφ in
/-- **The differential of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex, on stalks.** Under
`homTermStalkEquiv`, the map of stalks induced by the differential from degree `k` to degree
`k + 1` is, up to the sign `(-1)^{k+1}`, precomposition with the ring-level Koszul differential
`⋀^{k+1}((O_x)ʳ) ⟶ ⋀ᵏ((O_x)ʳ)` of the germs of the sequence. -/
theorem homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    (N : StructureSheafModules Rc) {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))
    (x : X)
    (y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n) x) :
    homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h' x (stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc)
        (cochain Rc K) ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d
          n m).val x y) =
      homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x ((m.negOnePow : ℤ) • y) ∘ₗ
        Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual fun i =>
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) k := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq _ y
  have hd : stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d n m).val x
          (germAt _ U x hxU s) =
      germAt _ U x hxU (((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d n m).val.app
          (op U) s) :=
    stalkLin_germAddHom _ U hxU s
  have hs : (m.negOnePow : ℤ) • germAt _ U x hxU s = germAt _ U x hxU (m.negOnePow • s) :=
    (map_zsmul (ConcreteCategory.hom (TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := Ab.{u})
      (commVal (Rc := Rc) ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n)).presheaf
          U x hxU)) _ _).symm.trans (congrArg _ (Units.smul_def _ _).symm)
  rw [hd, hs]
  refine Module.Basis.ext (wedgeBasis ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r (k + 1)) fun t => ?_
  have hw : (wedgeBasis ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r (k + 1)) t =
      exteriorPower.ιMulti ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) (k + 1)
        fun j => Pi.single (wedgeIndex (k + 1) t j) 1 :=
    wedgeBasis_apply ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r (k + 1) t
  have hdb := exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv_germ_dNat (Osharp := Rc) (A := A) (φ := φ) K f hφ k
    (x := x) U hxU (wedgeIndex (k + 1) t)
  have key := homTermIso_d_app_apply Rc K N h h' U U (𝟙 U) s
    (exteriorBasisSection A U (k + 1) (wedgeIndex (k + 1) t))
  conv_lhs => rw [wedgeBasis_eq_exteriorKoszulStalkEquiv_germ (A := A) Rc (k + 1) U hxU]
  refine (homTermStalkEquiv_germ Rc K N h' x U hxU _ _).trans ?_
  refine (congrArg (germAt N U x hxU) key).trans ?_
  refine (homTermStalkEquiv_germ Rc K N h x U hxU _ _).symm.trans ?_
  exact congrArg (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x (germAt _ U x hxU _)) (hdb.trans (hw ▸ rfl))

/-- A unit of `ℤ` acting twice is the identity. -/
private theorem units_zsmul_zsmul {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] (c : ℤˣ) (z : M) :
    (c : ℤ) • (c : ℤ) • z = z := by
  rw [smul_smul, Int.isUnit_mul_self c.isUnit, one_smul]

include hφ in
/-- A stalk of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex which the differential kills, read
through `homTermStalkEquiv`, is killed by precomposition with the ring-level Koszul
differential. -/
theorem homTermStalkEquiv_comp_d_eq_zero (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    (N : StructureSheafModules Rc) {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))
    (x : X)
    (y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.X n) x)
    (hy : stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc)
        (cochain Rc K) ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d
          n m).val x y = 0) :
    homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x y ∘ₗ
        Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual fun i =>
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) k = 0 := by
  have h₁ := homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d Rc f hφ K N h h' x ((m.negOnePow : ℤ) • y)
  rw [map_zsmul, hy, smul_zero, map_zero, units_zsmul_zsmul] at h₁
  exact h₁.symm

include hφ in
/-- Every precomposition of a functional on `⋀ᵏ((O_x)ʳ)` with the ring-level Koszul
differential is, through `homTermStalkEquiv`, the image under the differential of a stalk of the
Hom complex out of the Koszul complex. -/
theorem homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d_symm (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    (N : StructureSheafModules Rc) {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))
    (x : X)
    (ψ : ⋀[↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)]^k (Fin r → ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)) →ₗ[
      ringStalk Rc x] modStalk N x) :
    homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h' x (stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc)
        (cochain Rc K) ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj N)).obj.d
          n m).val x ((m.negOnePow : ℤ) • (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K N h x).symm ψ)) =
      ψ ∘ₗ Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual fun i =>
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) k := by
  rw [homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d Rc f hφ K N h h' x, units_zsmul_zsmul,
    LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- A stalk of the Hom complex into `O_Y` whose image under the stalk differential is, through
`homTermStalkEquiv`, a precomposition `χ ∘ d` with the ring-level Koszul differential has a
preimage under the differential. -/
private theorem exists_stalkLin_d_eq_of_dual_d_eq (hφ : ∀ k : Fin r,
    ((SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)).freeHomEquiv φ
      (ULift.up k)).val (op (⊤ : Opens ↥X)) = f k) (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (h' : m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (x : X)
    (y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X m) x)
    (χ : ⋀[↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)]^k
      (Fin r → ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)) →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x]
        ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x))
    (hχ : χ ∘ₗ Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual fun i =>
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) k =
      (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).toLinearMap ∘ₗ homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
        (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) h' x y) :
    ∃ z : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X n) x,
      stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.d n m).val x z = y := by
  refine ⟨_, (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K _ h' x).injective
    ((homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_d_symm Rc f hφ K _ h h' x
      ((unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ χ)).trans ?_)⟩
  refine LinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
  exact (congrArg (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).symm (LinearMap.congr_fun hχ w)).trans
    ((unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).symm_apply_apply _)

include hφ in
/-- **The Hom complex of the Koszul complex into `O_Y` is exact in the degrees `0, …, r - 1`.**
At a stalk its degree-`k` short complex is `Hom(⋀^{k-1}, O_x) ⟶ Hom(⋀ᵏ, O_x) ⟶ Hom(⋀^{k+1}, O_x)`
with differentials precomposition with the ring-level Koszul differential of the germs, up to
sign, and that complex is exact for a Koszul-regular sequence. -/
theorem exactAt_sheafHomComplex_unit (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    (hreg : ∀ x : X, Koszul.IsKoszulRegular fun i =>
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i))
    {n : ℤ} (hn₀ : 0 ≤ n) (hnr : n < r) :
    (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.ExactAt n := by
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k : ℕ, n = k := ⟨n.toNat, by omega⟩
  rw [HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff' _ ((k : ℤ) - 1) k ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) (by simp)
    (by simp), AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exact_iff_stalkShortComplex_exact]
  intro x
  rw [ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  change ∀ y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X (k : ℤ)) x,
    stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.d (k : ℤ) ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)).val x y = 0 →
    ∃ z : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X ((k : ℤ) - 1)) x,
      stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.d ((k : ℤ) - 1) (k : ℤ)).val x z = y
  intro y hy
  have h₂ : ((unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
      homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
        (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) rfl x y) ∘ₗ
        Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual fun i =>
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) k = 0 :=
    (LinearMap.comp_assoc _ _ _).trans ((congrArg _
      (homTermStalkEquiv_comp_d_eq_zero Rc f hφ K _ rfl rfl x y hy)).trans
        (LinearMap.comp_zero _))
  rcases k with _ | k
  · have h₃ := Koszul.dual_d_zero_eq_zero _ (hreg x) (by omega) _ h₂
    have h₄ : homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
        (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) rfl x y = 0 := by
      refine LinearMap.ext fun w => (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).injective ?_
      exact (LinearMap.congr_fun h₃ w).trans (map_zero _).symm
    refine ⟨0, ?_⟩
    rw [map_zero]
    exact ((homTermStalkEquiv Rc K _ rfl x).injective (h₄.trans (map_zero _).symm)).symm
  · obtain ⟨χ, hχ⟩ := Koszul.exists_dual_d_eq_of_comp_eq_zero _ (hreg x) (by omega) _ h₂
    have hk : ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1 = ((k : ℕ) : ℤ) := by omega
    exact exists_stalkLin_d_eq_of_dual_d_eq Rc f hφ K hk rfl x y χ hχ

/-- The differentials of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex into the quotient `O_X`
vanish, between any two degrees. -/
theorem sheafHomComplex_quotient_d_eq_zero (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (i j : ℤ) :
    (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
        (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))).obj.d i j = 0 := by
  by_cases h : i + 1 = j
  · subst h
    exact sheafHomComplex_d_eq_zero K i
  · exact HomologicalComplex.shape _ i j h

include hφ in
/-- **The ideal of germs is generated by the germs of the sequence.** -/
theorem stalkGermIdeal_le_span (x : X) :
    stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i =>
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) := by
  classical
  intro a ha
  obtain ⟨b, ⟨v, rfl⟩, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.1 ha
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulFreeStalkEquiv (Osharp := Rc) (r := r)
    x).symm.surjective v
  let L := (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).toLinearMap ∘ₗ stalkLin φ.val x ∘ₗ
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulFreeStalkEquiv (Osharp := Rc) (r := r) x).symm.toLinearMap
  have hL : ∀ i, L (Pi.single i 1) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i) := by
    intro i
    have hs : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulFreeStalkEquiv (Osharp := Rc) (r := r) x).symm
        (Pi.single i 1) = TopCat.Presheaf.germ (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r).val.presheaf ⊤ x
          (Opens.mem_top x) ((SheafOfModules.freeSection
            (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) (ULift.up i)).eval (op ⊤)) :=
      (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).2
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulFreeStalkEquiv_germ_freeSection ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) i).symm
    change unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x (stalkLin φ.val x
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.koszulFreeStalkEquiv (Osharp := Rc) (r := r) x).symm
        (Pi.single i 1))) = _
    rw [hs]
    exact (congrArg (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x)
      (stalkLin_germAddHom φ.val ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) _)).trans
      ((unitModuleStalkAddEquiv_germ Rc.obj x ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) _).trans
        (germ_unitScalar_freeSection f hφ ⊤ (Opens.mem_top x) i))
  change L c ∈ _
  rw [pi_eq_sum_univ c, map_sum]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
  rw [map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
  refine Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ?_
  have hi : (fun j => if i = j then (1 : ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)) else 0) =
      Pi.single i 1 := by
    funext j
    simp [Pi.single_apply, eq_comm]
  rw [hi, hL i]
  exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-- **The map of Hom complexes induced by `O_Y ⟶ O_X` is surjective termwise.** Each term of the
Koszul complex is free, so its Hom into `O_Y` maps onto its Hom into the quotient. -/
theorem epi_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_f (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ}
    (h : n = k) :
    Epi ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
        (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f n) := by
  refine (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.epi_iff_surjective_stalkMap _).2 fun x => ?_
  change Function.Surjective (stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
        (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f n).val x)
  intro t
  have hπ : Function.Surjective (stalkLin (koszulQuotientπ φ).val x) :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.epi_iff_surjective_stalkMap (koszulQuotientπ φ)).1
      inferInstance x
  have : Module.Free ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)
      (⋀[↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)]^k (Fin r → ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x))) :=
    Module.Free.of_basis (wedgeBasis ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x) r k)
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Module.projective_lifting_property (stalkLin (koszulQuotientπ φ).val x)
    (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K (quotient Rc (φ := φ)) h x t) hπ
  refine ⟨(homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
    (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) h x).symm g,
    (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K (quotient Rc (φ := φ)) h x).injective ?_⟩
  exact (homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_homMap Rc K (koszulQuotientπ φ) h x _).trans
    ((congrArg (stalkLin (koszulQuotientπ φ).val x ∘ₗ ·)
      (LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply _ g)).trans hg)

/-- A stalk of the Hom complex into `O_Y` killed by postcomposition with `O_Y ⟶ O_X` takes values
in the ideal of germs of the sequence, when read through `homTermStalkEquiv`. -/
private theorem unitEquiv_homTermStalkEquiv_mem_span (hφ : ∀ k : Fin r,
    ((SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)).freeHomEquiv φ
      (ULift.up k)).val (op (⊤ : Opens ↥X)) = f k) (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    {n : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (h : n = k) (x : X)
    (y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X n) x)
    (hy : stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f n).val x y = 0)
    (w : ⋀[↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x)]^k (Fin r → ↑(TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Rc.obj x))) :
    ((unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).toLinearMap ∘ₗ homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
        (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) h x y) w ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i =>
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i)) := by
  refine stalkGermIdeal_le_span Rc f hφ x ?_
  rw [← ker_quotientStalkMap]
  refine LinearMap.mem_ker.2 ?_
  refine (congrArg (stalkLin (koszulQuotientπ φ).val x)
    ((unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).symm_apply_apply _)).trans ?_
  have := (homTermStalkEquiv_stalkLin_homMap Rc K (koszulQuotientπ φ) h x y).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (homTermStalkEquiv Rc K (quotient Rc (φ := φ)) h x) hy).trans (map_zero _))
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun this w

include hφ in
/-- **The top-degree Hom complex sequence.** In degree `r ≥ 1`, the sequence
`𝓗om(⋀^{r-1}((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y) ⟶ 𝓗om(⋀^r((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y) ⟶ 𝓗om(⋀^r((O_Y)ʳ), O_X)`, the first map the
differential of the Hom complex and the second postcomposition with `O_Y ⟶ O_X`, is exact. At a
stalk, a functional on `⋀^r((O_x)ʳ)` with values in the ideal of germs is a precomposition with
the Koszul differential. -/
theorem exact_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_of_pos (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (hr : 0 < r) :
    (ShortComplex.mk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.d
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev (r : ℤ)) (r : ℤ))
      ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f (r : ℤ))
      (by rw [← HomologicalComplex.Hom.comm, sheafHomComplex_quotient_d_eq_zero,
        Limits.comp_zero])).Exact := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, r = m + 1 := ⟨r - 1, by omega⟩
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exact_iff_stalkShortComplex_exact]
  intro x
  rw [ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  change ∀ y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.X
            ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) x,
    stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)).val x y = 0 →
    ∃ z : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.X
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))) x,
      stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.d
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)).val x z = y
  intro y hy
  have hprev : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = ((m : ℕ) : ℤ) := by simp
  have hprev : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = ((m : ℕ) : ℤ) := by simp
  obtain ⟨χ, hχ⟩ := (Koszul.mem_span_iff_exists_dual_d_eq _ _).1
    (unitEquiv_homTermStalkEquiv_mem_span Rc f hφ K rfl x y hy)
  exact exists_stalkLin_d_eq_of_dual_d_eq Rc f hφ K hprev rfl x y χ hχ

include hφ in
/-- **The top-degree Hom complex sequence, for `r = 0`.** The sequence of
`exact_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_of_pos` is exact also for `r = 0`: then the ideal of germs is zero,
so postcomposition with `O_Y ⟶ O_X` is injective on `𝓗om(⋀⁰((O_Y)⁰), O_Y)`. -/
theorem exact_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_of_eq_zero (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) (hr : r = 0) :
    (ShortComplex.mk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.d
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev (r : ℤ)) (r : ℤ))
      ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f (r : ℤ))
      (by rw [← HomologicalComplex.Hom.comm, sheafHomComplex_quotient_d_eq_zero,
        Limits.comp_zero])).Exact := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exact_iff_stalkShortComplex_exact]
  intro x
  rw [ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  change ∀ y : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.X
            (r : ℤ)) x,
    stalkLin ((RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
          (koszulQuotientπ φ))).f (r : ℤ)).val x y = 0 →
    ∃ z : modStalk ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.X
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev (r : ℤ))) x,
      stalkLin ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)))).obj.d
            ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev (r : ℤ)) (r : ℤ)).val x z = y
  intro y hy
  have : IsEmpty (Fin r) := by rw [hr]; infer_instance
  have h₀ : homTermStalkEquiv Rc K
      (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) rfl x y = 0 := by
    refine LinearMap.ext fun w => (unitModuleStalkLinearEquiv Rc.obj x).injective ?_
    have hw := unitEquiv_homTermStalkEquiv_mem_span Rc f hφ K rfl x y hy w
    rw [Set.range_eq_empty, Ideal.span_empty, Ideal.mem_bot] at hw
    exact hw.trans (map_zero _).symm
  exact ⟨0, (map_zero _).trans
    ((homTermStalkEquiv Rc K _ rfl x).injective (h₀.trans (map_zero _).symm)).symm⟩

include hφ in
/-- **On the top cohomology sheaf, `O_Y ⟶ O_X` induces an isomorphism of Hom complexes.** In
degree `r ≥ 1` the Hom complex into `O_Y` vanishes above `r`, the Hom complex into `O_X` has
vanishing differential, and the map between them in degree `r` is a surjection whose kernel is
the image of the differential; so the map on the `r`-th cohomology sheaves is an isomorphism. -/
theorem isIso_homologyMap_homMap_koszulQuotientπ (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K))
      ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map (koszulQuotientπ φ)))
        (r : ℤ)) := by
  have := epi_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_f Rc K (rfl : (r : ℤ) = r)
  refine Stacks.HomologicalComplex.isIso_homologyMap_of_exact_of_epi _ _ ?_
    (sheafHomComplex_quotient_d_eq_zero Rc K _ _) (sheafHomComplex_quotient_d_eq_zero Rc K _ _)
    ((Nat.eq_zero_or_pos r).elim (exact_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_of_eq_zero Rc f hφ K)
      (exact_homMap_koszulQuotientπ_of_pos Rc f hφ K))
  exact (isZero_sheafHomComplex_unit_X_of_notMem_Icc Rc K (Or.inr (by simp))).eq_of_tgt _ _

/-- **The cochain-level identification of the Ext sheaves is natural in the coefficients.**
For a morphism of complexes `α : M ⟶ M'`, the map of Ext sheaves induced by `α` corresponds,
under `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain`, to the map on
cohomology sheaves induced by postcomposition with `α` on the Hom complexes out of the Koszul
complex. -/
theorem derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain_naturality (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    [QuasiIso K.augmentation] {M M' : CochainComplex (StructureSheafModules Rc) ℤ}
    (α : M ⟶ M') (n : ℤ) :
    derivedSheafExtMap Rc n (𝟙 _) (DerivedCategory.Q.map α) ≫
        (derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain Rc K M' n).hom =
      (derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain Rc K M n).hom ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
          (RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K)) α) n := by
  have hnat := Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyOfResolution_naturality_target
    Rc (cochain Rc K) M n (finite_not_isZero_cochain_X Rc K)
    (isFiniteFreeSummand_cochain_X Rc K) (cochainAugmentation Rc K) α
  have hcomm : derivedSheafExtMap Rc n (𝟙 _) (DerivedCategory.Q.map α) ≫
      (derivedSheafExtMapIso Rc n (DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)))
        (Iso.refl (DerivedCategory.Q.obj M'))).hom =
      (derivedSheafExtMapIso Rc n (DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)))
        (Iso.refl (DerivedCategory.Q.obj M))).hom ≫
      derivedSheafExtMap Rc n (𝟙 _) (DerivedCategory.Q.map α) :=
    (derivedSheafExtMap_comp Rc n _ _ _ _).trans
      ((congrArg₂ (fun k l => derivedSheafExtMap Rc n k l)
        ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm)
        ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm)).trans
        (derivedSheafExtMap_comp Rc n _ _ _ _).symm)
  exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans ((hcomm =≫ _).trans
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ((_ ≫= hnat).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm)))

include hφ in
/-- **The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient into the structure sheaf vanish outside the
degree `r`.** For an ideal sheaf `ℐ ⊂ O_Y` generated by global sections `f₁, …, f_r` whose germs
form a Koszul-regular sequence at every point, with quotient `O_X = O_Y/ℐ`,

`𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = 0` for every `n ≠ r`.

Outside `0, …, r` this is `isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc`. In the degrees
`0, …, r - 1` the Ext sheaf is the cohomology of the Hom complex out of the Koszul complex, which
is exact there by `exactAt_sheafHomComplex_unit`: at a stalk it is the dual of the Koszul
complex of a Koszul-regular sequence. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_ne (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    [QuasiIso K.augmentation]
    (hreg : ∀ x : X, Koszul.IsKoszulRegular fun i =>
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj (⊤ : Opens ↥X) x (Opens.mem_top x) (f i))
    {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ r) :
    IsZero (derivedSheafExt Rc
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (unitSingleComplex Rc)) n) := by
  rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with h | h
  · exact isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc Rc K (Or.inl h)
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hn with h' | h'
  · exact IsZero.of_iso (exactAt_sheafHomComplex_unit Rc f hφ K hreg h h').isZero_homology
      (structureSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain Rc K n)
  · exact isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc Rc K (Or.inr h')

include hφ in
/-- **In the degree `r`, the Ext sheaf into `O_Y` is the Ext sheaf into `O_X`.** For an ideal
sheaf `ℐ ⊂ O_Y` generated by global sections `f₁, …, f_r` whose Koszul complex resolves
`O_X = O_Y/ℐ`, the quotient map `O_Y ⟶ O_X` induces an isomorphism

`𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) ≅ 𝓔xt^r_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X)`.

No regularity of the germs is needed beyond the resolution. Both Ext sheaves are the `r`-th
cohomology sheaves of Hom complexes out of the Koszul complex, and the map between them is
`isIso_homologyMap_homMap_koszulQuotientπ` under the natural identification
`derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain_naturality`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafExtMap_unit_quotient (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    [QuasiIso K.augmentation] :
    IsIso (derivedSheafExtMap Rc (r : ℤ)
      (𝟙 (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))))
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map (koszulQuotientπ φ)))) := by
  have := isIso_homologyMap_homMap_koszulQuotientπ Rc f hφ K
  rw [(Iso.eq_comp_inv _).2 (derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain_naturality Rc K _ (r : ℤ))]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' (IsIso.comp_isIso' (Iso.isIso_hom _) this) (Iso.isIso_inv _)

end StalkComputation

end Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

